# CDP Audit — Chrome DevTools Protocol Diagnostics

## Overview

Diagnose and fix browser/web-app issues using CDP commands. Connects to headless Chrome via WebSocket (`ws://127.0.0.1:9222`) and uses CDP methods for full debugging control.

**ZES environment:** Headless Chromium on port 9222 (service: `chromium-cdp`). CDP Viewer UI at `:9223`.

## Prerequisites

- Chromium in headless mode with remote debugging on port 9222
- Python `websockets` library
- Or browser-use CLI (`browser-use`) for higher-level diagnostics

## Quick Start: Verify CDP is Alive

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9222/json/version | python3 -m json.tool
```

## CDP Viewer

A visual tab manager is available at **http://127.0.0.1:9223/** showing all open tabs with links to DevTools.

## Browser Diagnostics with browser-use

### Console Error Check
```bash
browser-use <<'PY'
new_tab("http://localhost:5050")
import time; time.sleep(2)
# Capture console logs from CDP
result = run_cdp("Runtime.evaluate", {"expression": "console.log('CDP audit check')"})
print("Page info:", page_info())
PY
```

### Full Dashboard Audit
```bash
browser-use <<'PY'
for name, url in [("Vite", "http://localhost:5050"), ("Next.js", "http://localhost:7070"), ("Control", "http://localhost:8083")]:
    new_tab(url)
    import time; time.sleep(2)
    info = page_info()
    print(f"{name}: {info.get('title','?')} — {info.get('status','?')}")
PY
```

## CDP Direct Commands

```python
# Get all console messages from a page
async with cdp_connect() as conn:
    await conn.execute("Runtime.enable")
    async for msg in conn.listen("Runtime.consoleAPICalled"):
        print(msg)
```

